Article 2 After a settlement agreement is reached, if any of the following circumstances exist, the People's Court may rule to suspend enforcement:
(1) all parties jointly submit a written settlement agreement to the People's Court;
(2) one party submits a written settlement agreement to the People's Court and the other parties approve it;
(3) the parties reach an oral settlement agreement and the enforcement personnel record the content of the settlement agreement in the transcript, which is signed or sealed by all parties.

Article 11 Where the applicant for enforcement applies for resumption of enforcement on the ground that the party subject to enforcement fails to perform the enforcement settlement agreement, and upon review by the People's Court, if the reason is established, the court shall rule to resume enforcement; under any of the following circumstances, the court shall rule not to resume enforcement:
(1) the application for resumption of enforcement is made after the enforcement settlement agreement has been fully performed;
(2) the performance period stipulated in the enforcement settlement agreement has not yet arrived, or the conditions for performance have not yet been met, except where the circumstances specified in Article 108 of the Contract Law are met;
(3) the party subject to enforcement is currently performing its obligations in accordance with the enforcement settlement agreement;
(4) other circumstances that do not meet the conditions for resumption of enforcement.

Article 19 During the enforcement process, if the party subject to enforcement raises an objection in accordance with Article 225 of the Civil Procedure Law based on a settlement agreement reached by the parties voluntarily but not submitted to the People's Court, or based on a settlement agreement submitted by one party to the People's Court but not approved by the other parties, the People's Court shall handle it separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) if the settlement agreement has been fully performed, rule to terminate the enforcement of the original effective legal instrument;
(2) if the performance period stipulated in the settlement agreement has not yet arrived, or the conditions for performance have not yet been met, rule to suspend enforcement, except where the circumstances specified in Article 108 of the Contract Law are met;
(3) if the party subject to enforcement is currently performing its obligations in accordance with the settlement agreement, rule to suspend enforcement;
(4) if the party subject to enforcement fails to perform the settlement agreement, rule to reject the objection;
(5) if the settlement agreement is not established, has not taken effect, or is void, rule to reject the objection.
